bg3le Ext.UI: never release into a torn-down UI; serialize with the View's input too, on by default

On top of 0001 and 0002. Two crashes in claude-run-2 (2026-10-10, research/impl-se.md):

- The recovery reload crashed in 0001's drain: a reference Lua took under the loading
  screen's View was given back after that View was freed, and the element's teardown
  (TimerTrigger::OnDetaching -> AttachableObject::GetView()->CancelTimer) called into it.
  Now each held reference records the UI generation it was taken in. The generation moves
  on when the View is replaced and when the client state enters or leaves anything but
  Running/Save/Paused (game_state.cpp); the queue is dropped then, and a release from an
  older generation, while the UI is not settled, or of an object that no longer looks
  alive is leaked instead (counted).
- A SIGSEGV in Panel::UpdateChildrenZOrder under Mouse::Move (the UI thread's hit test,
  outside View::Update) while Lua walked the tree from the client thread: both rebuild a
  Panel's lazy z-order cache. The View's input entry points (mouse, wheel, keys, Char,
  and their IView thunks) now hold 0002's frame lock too, and serializing is on by
  default (BG3LE_UI_SERIALIZE=0 turns it off). The UI thread waits at most 16 ms for the
  lock, as Lua waits at most 50 ms, so neither can deadlock on a game lock.
- Ext._Internal.UiSerialize() returns on, Lua timeouts, UI timeouts, generation, leaked.

Against bg3le 3728a68 (v0.3.6) with 0001 and 0002. Applied by tools/build_bg3le.sh.
